{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.admissible_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.admissible_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AfreeThetaConstraint.lean#L165-L173","doc":"The admissibility hypothesis holds for every sufficiently large `A`, so the\nfamily of solutions above is a genuine continuum rather than an isolated point:\nraising `A` only ever makes more assignments available\n(`thetaSq_nonneg_mono` is the two-anchor form of the same monotonicity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.exists_angle_assignment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.exists_angle_assignment","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AfreeThetaConstraint.lean#L139-L163","doc":"**Adding anchors never helps: the system is underdetermined by exactly one\nat EVERY anchor count.**\n\nEach new anchor contributes one equation `S_i = A·κ·(ln²q₀ − ϑ_i²)` *and* one\nnew unknown `ϑ_i`. So `n` anchors give `n` equations in `n + 1` unknowns\n(`A` together with the `n` angles) — a deficit of one, independent of `n`.\n\nThis states the consequence constructively: for **every** admissible `A` there\nis a complete angle assignment solving all `n` equations simultaneously. `A` is\ntherefore never pinned, no matter how many anchors are collected. The\nunderdetermination is STRUCTURAL, not a shortage of data.\n\nThe only escape is an anchor whose `ϑ` is fixed *independently* — an equation\ncarrying no new unknown. The corpus's one candidate, the electron/trefoil `3₁`\nwith `Vol = 0`, is closed on its own terms: a torus knot's Kashaev invariant\ngrows polynomially rather than exponentially, so it has no Stokes constant to\nsupply an `S` at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.ratio_unconstrained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.ratio_unconstrained","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AfreeThetaConstraint.lean#L127-L133","doc":"Restated as the design constraint: the channel places **no** restriction on\nthe ratio of the two `ϑ`. Every value above 1 occurs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.ratio_attained","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.ratio_attained","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AfreeThetaConstraint.lean#L92-L125","doc":"**Every ratio is attainable — the unfalsifiability of ratio-shaped\ncandidates.**\n\nGiven a positive leak `S₁ > 0`, a negative leak `S₂ < 0`, and *any* target\nratio `y > 1`, the explicit value\n\n  `A = (y·S₁ − S₂) / (κ · ln²q₀ · (y − 1))`\n\nis positive and satisfies `ϑ₂² = y · ϑ₁²` with `ϑ₁² > 0` — i.e. it is an\nadmissible point of the family, with both `ϑ` real.\n\nConsequence: a route supplying only the **ratio** `ϑ₂/ϑ₁` can never be\nrefuted by the channel. Whatever ratio it produces, some `A` realises it\nexactly, with zero residual. Such a route does not test `A_ω`; it merely\nrenames it. A genuine test requires **both** `ϑ` absolutely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.A_determined_of_theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.A_determined_of_theta","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AfreeThetaConstraint.lean#L71-L81","doc":"**A route landing on the curve determines `A`.** Given a `ϑ` obtained\nindependently — not by inverting the channel — the channel returns `A`\nrather than consuming it. This is what would make an independent leg a\n*determination* of `A_ω` instead of a literature import. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.afree_invariant_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.afree_invariant_div","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AfreeThetaConstraint.lean#L63-L69","doc":"The same relation in quotient form, when the second leak is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.afree_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.afree_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AfreeThetaConstraint.lean#L52-L61","doc":"**The `A`-free invariant.** Eliminating `A` (and `κ`) between the two anchor\nequations leaves a relation between the two `ϑ` and the two measured `S` alone.\n\nThis is the falsifiable content of the channel: a curve in the `(ϑ₁, ϑ₂)` plane\nthat any independent determination must land on, with no conditioning on `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.lnq_sq_sub_thetaSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AfreeThetaConstraint.lnq_sq_sub_thetaSq","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AfreeThetaConstraint.lean#L47-L50","doc":"Reading the channel backwards: `ln²q₀ − ϑ² = S/(Aκ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}